## Native executor — 08/11/2026

| Tool/version | Official source | Decision / unresolved |
|---|---|---|
| Docker 29.7.2 observed | [create/start lifecycle](https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/docker/container/create/) | Create separately, attach streams, inspect state then remove own UUID container. |
| Playwright 1.56.1 | [native CLI](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/playwright/v1.56.1/packages/playwright/src/program.ts) | Forward native argv to prepared CLI; no legacy staging restriction. |
| Playwright current documentation; recipe 1.56.1 | [Browsers and system dependencies](https://playwright.dev/docs/docker) | Build browser dependencies explicitly; compatibility on Debian remains unverified. |
| Trivy 0.76.2 | [DB flags and conflicts](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aquasecurity/trivy/v0.76.2/pkg/flag/db_flags.go) | Skip-update and download-only conflict; maintenance caller must override env defaults explicitly. |
| Trivy 0.76.2 | [Connectivity](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aquasecurity/trivy/v0.76.2/docs/guide/advanced/air-gap.md) | DB, Java DB, checks and VEX are different resources; no claim of universal offline readiness. |
| Ruff 0.11.13 | [configuration and fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh/ruff/0.11.13/docs/configuration.md) | Native config and fix remain consumer choices; writable project is explicit. |
| YARA-X 1.0.0 | [release asset digest and format](https://api.github.com/repos/VirusTotal/yara-x/releases/tags/v1.0.0) | Tar gzip (despite .gz suffix) needs content detection and extraction; official digest recorded, Docker operation still blocked. |
| CodeQL 2.27.3 | [bundle packs](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.27.3) | Use whole bundle with extractors/runtime/packs, native entrypoint; no global application build dependencies. |
| CodeQL 2.27.3 | [Linux64 bundle SHA256](https://api.github.com/repos/github/codeql-action/releases/tags/codeql-bundle-v2.27.3) | Official artifact digest recorded; builder compares downloaded bytes before build. |
| CodeQL current setup for selected bundle | [Bundle and license](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/how-tos/find-and-fix-code-vulnerabilities/scan-from-the-command-line/set-up-codeql-cli) | Use glibc Debian; applicable license conditions remain consumer/operator responsibility. |

## Acesso ao socket e integração — 08/11/2026

| Fonte | Seção | Uso e limite |
|---|---|---|
| [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/linux-postinstall/) | Non-root access and session refresh | Group database differs from active process credentials; apply host administration only when appropriate. |
| [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/engine/daemon/troubleshoot/) | Daemon and client endpoint checks | Separate denied connection from stopped daemon; verify docker info, context and host. |
| [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/) | Docker daemon attack surface | Access to rootful daemon is privileged; do not expose socket globally or unauthenticated TCP. |
| [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/rootless/) | Rootless prerequisites and endpoint | Separate daemon is an alternative requiring explicit compatibility and data migration review. |
| [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/docker/context/use/) | Context selection and environment | Docker context use changes persistent default; per-process context may differ. |
| [Linux man-pages](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/user_namespaces.7.html) | UID/GID maps and unmapped IDs | Namespace credentials and displayed nobody IDs do not establish host socket permission. |
| [openSUSE](https://en.opensuse.org/SDB:Docker) | Distribution installation instructions | Page returned HTTP 403; no distribution-specific install procedure claimed. |

